<title>FRANCE: France moves to let Europeans vote in local polls.</title>
<headline>France moves to let Europeans vote in local polls.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French cabinet on Wednesday approved a bill to allow nationals from European Union countries living in France to vote and stand in municipal elections as provided by the Maastricht treaty.</p>
<p>The bill, to be put to parliament, will allow EU nationals to sit on town councils but not as mayors or deputy mayors.</p>
<p>Government spokeswoman Catherine Trautmann told a news conference France was the only EU country not to have implemented the measure, which was approved by the European Parliament in December 1994.</p>
</text>
